    "name": "Tanzanian Tangerine Iris Rhizome (Bulb)",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The Tanzanian Tangerine iris is&nbsp;a Tall Bearded (TB) iris, 38 inches tall, with a plicata flower type, featuring radiant deep tangerine standards and tannish orange falls with a red wine-stippled overlay and light orange beards.&nbsp;Introduced by Brad Kasperek in 1995, this ruffled, flared flower blooms early to mid-season and is known for its unique, warm color combination and strong, well-branched stalks.</span></p>",
